From 25a3dffd494c7777357465824870a8ea85f89ce3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:29:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] Give LeaseReader an explicit local-verifier chain
 authority

authority 'verifier' reads through ONE local validating endpoint (patched Helios:
sequencer-signed unsafe head, proof-backed state, maintained Base EVM): a
confirmed block below the verifier head, never behind an accepted block, fresh by
maxBlockAgeMs, read through a client pinned to that block hash that offers only
proof-backed methods and refuses everything else by name, re-checked for
reorganization, all within one deadline. No provider client exists in this mode,
so failures refuse. Legacy quorum stays the default and is labelled as provider
agreement. Settlement and bandwidth reads at a snapshot's own block go through
new reader primitives (blockHashIs, readAt) that keep the two-client rule in
quorum mode. Host admission, wg-provider, directory and management hosts accept
chainAuthority/chainVerifier (or ENCLAVE_CHAIN_AUTHORITY/ENCLAVE_CHAIN_VERIFIER).

(cherry picked from commit 921d60c2b37ec8ae64e1fd22d7bc7b408939bd70)
